# KISS FFT (double) as a static library: complex and real FFTs with C math library calls from an archive member.
# kissfft_main.c runs forward and inverse complex FFTs of four mixed-radix
# sizes and real FFTs of the even ones and prints rounded fixed-point hashes.
# libkiss.a's kiss_fft.c calls cos, sin, floor and sqrt, which the MSIL link
# binds to the C math library, and malloc, which comes from the support archive
# in the MSIL build; -ffp-contract=off keeps the native build free of fused
# multiply-adds, so both builds round alike.
# Built as a multi-TU program with static archives (%{msil_archives}: one per
# library plus libsup.a, the support library of ../support) from the corpus
# cache (%{msil_corpus}, filled by msil/utils/corpus/fetch.py), with the shim
# headers of ../shim in both builds (%{msil_copts}), at every level of the leg,
# and compared with the native build of the same sources; the error count is
# the exit status, so the transcript ends [exit 0]. Plan 5.12.9 (M23).
# ../det/kissfft.test repeats these REDEFINE lines for %{msil_det}.
# REQUIRES: msil-corpus-kissfft
# REDEFINE: %{msil_srcs} = %S/../kissfft/kissfft_main.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_archives} = kiss=%{msil_corpus}/kissfft-2a1f1337160e/kiss_fft.c, \
# REDEFINE:   %{msil_corpus}/kissfft-2a1f1337160e/kiss_fftr.c;sup=%S/../support/sup_arena.c, \
# REDEFINE:   %S/../support/sup_malloc.c,%S/../support/sup_memcmp.c,%S/../support/sup_memset.c, \
# REDEFINE:   %S/../support/sup_memcpy.c,%S/../support/sup_strlen.c,%S/../support/sup_out.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_copts} = -isystem %S/../shim -I%S/../support \
# REDEFINE:   -I%{msil_corpus}/kissfft-2a1f1337160e -DNDEBUG -Dkiss_fft_scalar=double \
# REDEFINE:   -ffp-contract=off -Werror=implicit-function-declaration -w
# RUN: %{msil_prog}
